Subject: [PATCH 25/25] feat(license): request and activation files as
 password-protected zips, the password derived from the file name

VERSION: 1.0 (2026-10-17)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0024)

Both files that travel between the customer and the vendor are now a .zip
with one AES-256 encrypted entry (WinZip AE-2: 7-Zip, WinRAR, Windows 11).
The file name holds no customer data, only a random token:
  KMS-<TOKEN>.zip            TOKEN = 16 characters A-Z, 2-7
and the zip password comes from it:
  printf %s TOKEN | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac KMS-ZIP-1 | awk '{print $NF}' | cut -c1-32
(kms-license.mjs 1.3: `node kms-license.mjs password FILE.zip`). A browser
adding " (1)" to the name does no harm; removing the KMS-... part does.

- License page, "Download license request": KMS-<TOKEN>.zip holding
  license-request.kmsreq (still X25519-encrypted for the vendor inside).
- License page, "Open activation file": accepts only a .zip; the new
  admin-only API license.unzip opens it and fills the activation code box.
- server/license/zip.ts replaces the yazl helper of patch 0022.

